   "subject": "Re: need help with contour plot",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Generally speaking, with ggplot you want all your variables in a\r<br>single data frame, and then you tell ggplot your data, aesthetic\r<br>mappings, and geom to use. So for example, in this case could do:\r<br>\r<br>library(reshape)\r<br>zdf &lt;- melt(z)\r<br>zdf &lt;- cbind(zdf,expand.grid(1:length(x),1:length(y)))\r<br>\r<br>library(ggplot2)\r<br>ggplot(zdf,aes(Var1,Var2))+geom_raster(aes(fill=value))\r<br>\r<br>This basically duplicates the filled.contour output.\r<br>\r<br>Ben\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "\r<br>\r<br>On Fri, Mar 21, 2014 at 10:31 AM,  &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">phi...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:\r<br>&gt; Hi everybody!\r<br>&gt; I am struggling with ggplot. Here is what I want to do.\r<br>&gt; I want to produce a contour plot, but not with using filled.contour as shown\r<br>&gt; below, but with ggplot (because it looks much better).\r<br>&gt; I know that it is possible, but I cannot get it running. Here z has the\r<br>&gt; dimensions of x*y and should be represented in terms of colours.\r<br>&gt; Does anybody have an example for that? I have also posted this in a R-forum,\r<br>&gt; but without success. Thanks!\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; x&lt;-as.matrix(read.table(file=&quot;<a href=\"http://www.color-space.de/webseiten/upload/dl/forum/x.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.color-space.de/webseiten/upload/dl/forum/x.txt&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792371035818000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0VpDaM4yFrkv0sm4qI4eLD\">http://www.color-space.de/webseiten/upload/dl/forum/x.txt</a>&quot;,\r<br>&gt; dec = &quot;.&quot;))\r<br>&gt; y&lt;-as.matrix(read.table(file=&quot;<a href=\"http://www.color-space.de/webseiten/upload/dl/forum/y.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.color-space.de/webseiten/upload/dl/forum/y.txt&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792371035818000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1b1Tj6kT8eDf0f1sB0aN4H\">http://www.color-space.de/webseiten/upload/dl/forum/y.txt</a>&quot;,\r<br>&gt; dec = &quot;.&quot;))\r<br>&gt; z&lt;-as.matrix(read.table(file=&quot;<a href=\"http://www.color-space.de/webseiten/upload/dl/forum/z.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.color-space.de/webseiten/upload/dl/forum/z.txt&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792371035818000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0fqDRrrwC9XSwy0JwASjG_\">http://www.color-space.de/webseiten/upload/dl/forum/z.txt</a>&quot;,\r<br>&gt; dec = &quot;.&quot;))\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; filled.contour(x,y,z)\r<br>&gt;\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
